# Keep the build context small and secrets out of the image.
node_modules
dist
.git
.gitignore
.env
review.env
visual-handoff.json
visual-pulled-base.json
*.log
# Gitignored scratch space some checkouts keep beside the sources — never image
# content, and it can be large enough to slow the build context down on its own.
.docs-local

# Host STATE, never image content (#101). `COPY . .` in the builder would bake a
# developer's `.data/meta.db` — password hashes and all — into a layer, and the
# boot guard would then find that dead copy at /app/.data and refuse to start.
# `docker/` below already covers `docker/volumes/`.
.data
backups

# Test/build output that only ever flows the other way. `make save` drops its
# tarball at the repo root, and it is the image — copying it back in is circular.
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
notarium-*.tar.gz
test/visual/**/*.png

# Tooling/docs that the image doesn't need. Only the image-native operator CLI
# from `docker/` is runtime content; compose files, host volumes and this build
# metadata stay outside the context.
Makefile
docker/*
!docker/notarium-cli
scripts
# …except the two scripts invoked by manifest hooks inside the image build: the
# dependency freshness recorder runs before the source COPY, while the SPA size gate
# hangs off the web workspace's build script. Without either file the manifest-only
# cache prefix or the later `npm run build` cannot complete.
!scripts/checkup/depsFreshness.mjs
!scripts/checkWebBundleBudget.mjs
README.md
# Keep LICENSE / NOTICE / COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md / THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the
# build context: the runtime stage copies the corpus for an image recipient.
